WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.792
A data audit is the first systematic look at an unfamiliar dataset.

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:09.027
Before we clean, we want to understand the structure.

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:15.367
Start with the shape to see how many rows and columns you have.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.162
Check the data types. Look at a few rows.

00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:24.510
Count missing values. For categorical columns, inspect the unique values or value counts.

00:00:25.287 --> 00:00:28.879
Run the code and look carefully at what Pandas reports.

00:00:28.879 --> 00:00:32.159
Do not focus only on whether the code runs.

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:34.764
Ask what each output tells you.

00:00:34.764 --> 00:00:42.989
For example, if amount is stored as an object instead of a numeric type, that is a clue that the column may contain text

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:45.024
or inconsistent values.

00:00:45.024 --> 00:00:52.679
If the region column contains North, north, and north with spaces, those may represent the same category but appear as

00:00:52.679 --> 00:01:00.287
different groups. A good audit gives you a list of issues to investigate before you start changing the data.
